# the object's debug records as DWARF 5 debugging information
#
# a compile unit describes each section the records name: a section holding a
# function's code, a located global or a line sequence. mirl places each
# function and each global in a section of its own, so a unit is one item,
# and a section holding several functions is one unit of them all. where the
# format ties a section to the section it describes, each unit's
# contributions are sections of their own owned by the unit's section, so a
# link that drops the section drops its debugging information with it:
# .debug_info, a line table of its own in .debug_line, and .debug_loclists
# and .debug_rnglists when it has a list. elsewhere each contribution is
# appended to the object's section of its kind, and the object has a list
# section only where a unit writes a list. what every unit names is held
# once per object in sections owned by none, which a link keeps whatever it
# drops: the abbreviations, the line strings, the object's unit, its own type
# units, and the object's line table, a header of every file. nothing they
# hold names a unit, and a unit names nothing in another unit, so no unit a
# link keeps refers to one it dropped.
#
# a unit's entry states its language, producer, name and directory, each name
# a DW_FORM_line_strp into the line strings, its code by DW_AT_low_pc and
# DW_AT_high_pc over one function, or by a range list over several, and its
# line table by DW_AT_stmt_list. a unit's line table lists the files the unit
# names, the object's first file first, and holds the sequences of its
# section. the object's unit names the object's line table, whose file k + 1
# is the object's file k. a unit's children are the
# abstract entry of every callee inlined in it, then each function with its
# variables and the code inlined in it, with no children for a function of
# neither, then each global. the object's unit holds every type a unit's
# entry names, each type those name until every type named is written, and
# each global with no place. a variable, parameter or global names its type
# by DW_FORM_ref_addr, its entry's offset in .debug_info relocated against the
# object's unit, and a type names another by DW_FORM_ref4 within its unit,
# filled once every type is written. a structure, union, tagged union or
# enumeration with a key is described once in a program: the object it is
# the own type of writes it as a type unit after the object's unit, one
# another object describes is a declaration naming that unit's signature
# (DW_AT_signature), and a shared one, which every object naming it describes
# alike, is a type unit of its own in a section of its own, in a group whose
# signature is the unit's, where the format's links keep one copy of a group
# of sections by its signature, and is written in each unit that names it
# elsewhere. every unit that names a type unit other than its own holds a
# declaration of it naming its signature, which is the hash of the type's key
# alone, so every object names it alike without describing it. a tagged union
# is a structure of its discriminant and a variant part of its cases.
#
# every address is written in place, a datum of the address width relocated
# against the mark or symbol it names. a location or range list is named by
# DW_FORM_sec_offset, relocated against its unit's list section past the
# section's header. over code of fixed size a location list states each range
# by its offsets from its function's start, which is the unit's base address
# in a unit of one function and a DW_LLE_base_address otherwise, and a range
# list an inlined range by its offsets likewise or by its start and length
# (DW_RLE_offset_pair, DW_RLE_start_length). over code the linker may resize
# each range states its two addresses (DW_LLE_start_end, DW_RLE_start_end). a
# variable in one place over all of its function's code is located by an
# expression alone. a variable's location list has an entry per range where
# DWARF can state where it is, so a debugger reads it as optimised out
# elsewhere: a frame slot or a webassembly location with steps over it is one
# DWARF's expressions do not state. a global is at its symbol's address, a
# thread-local at its symbol's offset in its thread's block before
# DW_OP_form_tls_address in the form the format's row states, with no
# location where the object's relocations write none of the row's kinds, and
# one another unit defines is a declaration. a declaration's file and line,
# and the unit's DW_AT_stmt_list, are written where the object has line
# records. every reference between the sections is an offset relocated by
# the section-relative kind against the start of the section it names. the
# encoding is 32-bit DWARF.

